# .prettierignore: what the formatter must not touch.
#
# Scope is deliberate: this repo formats CODE only (.js, .vue, .css). Markdown,
# JSON and HTML are excluded, so prose and machine-parsed files keep whatever
# shape their consumers expect. See the "Formatting" section of CLAUDE.md.

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
dist/
client/dist/

# Dev state, local databases, scratch space
data/
server/data/
tmp/
screenshots/
backup/
*.log

# Test harness run artifacts (can contain install-time secrets)
scripts/test-harness/results/

# Prose: docs and release notes are hand-formatted. RELEASE-NOTES.md headings
# are machine-parsed by scripts/build-releases-manifest.js, which requires the
# literal "## vX.Y.Z — YYYY-MM-DD" form including the em-dash. Reflowing these
# buys nothing and risks the release pipeline.
*.md

# Machine-consumed data. Reformatting a lockfile is pure churn, and
# scripts/test-harness/manifest.json is read by agents against a fixed shape.
*.json

# Markup: client/index.html is a Vite entry template, left as authored.
*.html

# CI definitions. Reformatting these is machine-visible risk for no gain, and
# they sit outside the js/vue/css scope this config commits to.
*.yml
*.yaml
